From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/lima: Register the devfreq cooling device with an energy model

lima registers its cooling device without an energy model, so the
power allocator governor cannot budget the GPU: on a board whose
thermal zone binds the GPU as a cooling device, only the CPU is
throttled, and the GPU keeps its top OPP past the control temperature.

Register it with devfreq_cooling_em_register(), as panfrost and panthor
do. The energy model comes from the OPP table and the device's
dynamic-power-coefficient; without that property the cooling device is
registered as before.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_devfreq.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_devfreq.c
@@ -166,7 +166,7 @@
 
 	ldevfreq->devfreq = devfreq;
 
-	cooling = of_devfreq_cooling_register(dev->of_node, devfreq);
+	cooling = devfreq_cooling_em_register(devfreq, NULL);
 	if (IS_ERR(cooling))
 		dev_info(dev, "Failed to register cooling device\n");
 	else
